// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO48 tagged "led_high" - confirmed onboard amber
// LED_BUILTIN (shared with SPI SCK/D13; homeding.github.io Nano ESP32
// reference: "switched on by providing HIGH on GPIO48"). GPIO46/0/45
// tagged "led_r_low"/"led_g_low"/"led_b_low" - confirmed onboard RGB
// LED (LED_RED/LED_GREEN/LED_BLUE), active-low (homeding.github.io:
// "switched on...by pulling the GPIO lines to LOW"; corroborated by
// Arduino forum "Default Nano ESP32 RGB LED Sketch" thread).
{
  "boardName": "ESP32S3",
